# Chrome's own computed accessibility tree of the graph canvas (dynamics
# grammar plan, G9, F68). This receipt carries the scenario runner's one
# stated exception to "no DevTools": the runner attaches to this receipt's
# Chrome over the DevTools protocol once the scenario is done, read-only and
# never sending input, and reads Accessibility.getFullAXTree for the canvas's
# slot, its items and their Drag and Pin buttons. The page's own semantic tree
# is asserted by p4_tree_canvas_reader.scn; this one asserts nothing about the
# buttons itself, so its positive control (?plant_a11y=missing_action) must be
# caught by Chrome's tree alone.
assert snap ready == true
settle 3
assert snap reader-canvas ~ shown
log canvas reader devtools receipt complete
